## 6. Runtime Acceptance and Unofficial Builds

By entering an administration password, clicking Start, Unlock, Sign In,
Agree, or Connect, or otherwise using a released client or server, the user
confirms that the user reviewed and accepted this License, the linked Terms of
Use and Privacy Policy, the applicable Third-Party Materials notices, and the
responsibility obligations above.

An unofficial build may be compiled by a user for Personal Use, but it is not
an OpenStorey release, is not covered by OpenStorey signing or support, and
must not be presented as official. A build-access or electronic-signature
workflow at `sign.autoyou.me` may be used to document authorization for an
Official Build. It does not disclose or transfer signing keys, private network
details, or private source code to the signer. Approval records may be sent to
`build@autoyou.me` and retained as evidence of the agreed artifact scope.

